---
description: OpenAthlete – Backend (NestJS) Architecture & Controllers/Services
globs:
  - "apps/api/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Stack: NestJS 11, `nestjs-zod`, CASL, Socket.IO.

- Modules & layering:
  - Domain modules under `src/modules`. Core HTTP surface in `core/controllers`, logic in `core/services`.
  - Import `AuthModule`, inject `PrismaService` where needed. Map DB to camelCase for frontend.

- Controllers:
  - Validate input with `ZodValidationPipe` using DTO schemas from `@openathlete/shared`.
  - Guard authenticated routes with `@UseGuards(AuthGuard('jwt'), UserTypeGuard)`; get user via `@JwtUser()`.

- Services:
  - Use PrismaService directly (no repository pattern). Inject PrismaService and call Prisma methods directly (e.g., `this.prisma.model.create()`, `this.prisma.model.findMany()`, etc.).
  - Keep business rules and CASL ability checks here.
  - Use shared mappers (`keysToCamel`, etc.) where relevant. Strong typing end-to-end; avoid partials without proper types.

- Realtime & agents:
  - Socket.IO interactions under `src/modules/agent`. Keep event payloads typed.

- When adding endpoints (backend steps):
  1) Add route in controller; validate using shared Zod schema.
  2) Implement service method; perform CASL checks; return mapped data.
  3) Ensure DTOs/types are from `@openathlete/shared`.
